#: ../../../reference/interfaces/media-control-interface.md:2
msgid "media-control interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/media-control-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"The `media-control` interface permits access to media control devices and "
"Video4Linux (V4L) devices via the Linux kernel's [Media Controller API]"
"(https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/userspace-api/media/mediactl/media-"
"controller.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/media-control-interface.md:9
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/media-control-interface.md:11
msgid "**Auto-connect**: no"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/media-control-interface.md:13
msgid ""
"The kernel media controller API allows connecting and configuring media "
"hardware subsystems. These operations should be considered privileged since "
"the driver assumes trusted input, and therefore this interface requires "
"manual connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/media-control-interface.md:15
msgid "Code examples"
msgstr ""

